<div id="study-overview" class="rounded-panel border border-line dark:border-line-on-dark bg-surface dark:bg-surface-on-dark p-6 lg:p-8 flex flex-col gap-5">
  <%# Said out loud, and on the heading's own line as the board has it, because
      the order is the point: the registry's own words are what you read, and the
      plain-language rewrite below is something you ask for. Without the label
      the two blocks look interchangeable. %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
    <%= render Typography::HeadingComponent.new(size: :h5, text: "What this study is testing") %>
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.09em] text-ink-3 dark:text-ink-3-on-dark">
      From the registry record
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# Unedited and in full, as on the board, rather than the detailed description
      sitting behind the dropdown it used to. Its density is the argument for the
      rewrite offered underneath it, and a reader who never opens the dropdown
      never sees why that offer is there. Most run to a couple of paragraphs; the
      long tail is exactly the case the rewrite exists for. %>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 font-body leading-relaxed text-ink-2 dark:text-ink-2-on-dark">
    <% (helpers.prose_paragraphs(summary) + helpers.prose_paragraphs(detailed_description)).each do |paragraph| %>
      <p><%= paragraph %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# The board's chip row. Its own chips are the study's design, which the
      registry does give but which "What taking part involves" already says in
      sentences further down the page. These are the conditions, which are the
      answer to the heading and appear nowhere else on it. %>
  <% if conditions.present? %>
    <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-label="Conditions this study covers">
      <% conditions.each do |condition| %>
        <li class="rounded-card bg-surface-2 dark:bg-navy-900/40 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-ink-2 dark:text-ink-2-on-dark">
          <%= condition %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  <% end %>

  <%# After the source text, not before it. This used to render between the
      summary and the detailed description, so the rewrite appeared above half
      of what it was rewriting. %>
  <%= helpers.turbo_stream_from "readable_study_summary_#{nct_id}" %>
  <div id="readable-study-summary-content-<%= nct_id %>">
    <%= helpers.render partial: "shared/readable_study_summary_content", locals: {record: readable_summary, nct_id: nct_id, source_present: source_present?} %>
  </div>
</div>
